      "side": 1,
      "message": "The CLI runs the formatter but not the project\u0027s `remove_trailing_whitespaces` save action (`.settings/org.eclipse.jdt.ui.prefs`). Verified against Eclipse on the same fixture: when the formatter inserts a blank line before Javadoc root tags it emits `\\t * ` with a trailing space; Eclipse strips it on save, the CLI does not. So `--write` can introduce trailing whitespace Eclipse wouldn\u0027t, and `--check` accepts both forms.\n\nMirror the save action by stripping trailing horizontal whitespace before returning:\n\n```java\nprivate static final Pattern TRAILING_WS \u003d Pattern.compile(\"[ \\\\t]+(?\u003d\\\\R|\\\\z)\");\n...\nreturn TRAILING_WS.matcher(document.get()).replaceAll(\"\");\n```",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "ae3bf2737d829bb23fadf2dbbd682bfa5c1b97fc",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
